        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF148 Iterator.zip(), Iterator.zipKeyed()]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28960</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28960"/>
        <updated>2026-02-03T03:07:49.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF148 ships the TC39 <a href="https://github.com/tc39/proposal-joint-iteration">joint iteration</a> proposal in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2003333" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2003333</a> - that adds two methods to Iterator - zip and zipKeyed.</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds features for both. These don't show up in Chrome and Safari yet. Searching doesn't show evidence they are in Bun, Deno, NodeJS yet - I haven't tested though. Have set to false.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3805369463" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42743" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42743/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42743">mdn/content#42743</a></p>]]></content>
