    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF148 Document.execCommand with paste supported in content]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28953</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28953"/>
        <updated>2026-02-03T00:57:32.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF148 Supports using Document.execCommand with option "paste" in web content in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998195#c18" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1998195#c18</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Previously this would only work on extensions. The change is a reimplementation of the feature using the Clipboard API, so shares the same behaviour as added in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3699897493" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28587" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28587">#28587</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The feature is non-standard but in its "kind of" standard, paste is only supported in extensions. So what we're doing is adding non-standard behaviour to some browsers. What I have done is added an entry for paste that matches <code class="notranslate">copy</code> and similar in versions, then added version notes for this additional "non-standard" implementation.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3805383037" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42747" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/42747/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42747">mdn/content#42747</a></p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>hamishwillee</name>
            <email>hamishwillee@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/hamishwillee</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-02-02T06:05:23.000Z</published>
    </entry>
